unty"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids in Prince George&rsquo;s County came in under 90% of normal in September to October in 40 of 75 years since 1951. In 2025 the middle ran 48% of normal in October to November and 43% in November to December. So far in 2026 it has run 53% in March to April and 65% in April to May. Every grid had its driest year in 1965, with grid 23014 lowest at 69%.</p>"}
